WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
- I just bought a total
stranger's diary off the internet.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.551
Oh, God!

00:00:04.551 --> 00:00:05.960
She's inside my head.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.292
This is going badly.

00:00:07.292 --> 00:00:09.875
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.980
One weird thing you can buy on eBay

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.889
is a stranger's diary.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:20.628
You can bid on a total stranger's
most personal thoughts.

00:00:20.628 --> 00:00:22.679
Most of the diaries you find on eBay

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:25.959
are from 50 to 100 years ago or more.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:29.188
But I want to see if I can
find a diary from recent times,

00:00:29.188 --> 00:00:31.996
something that was written
in like the last 20 years.

00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:35.579
Okay, I found a diary
from the early 2000s.

00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:39.457
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:41.756
It's from 2001 to 2005,

00:00:41.756 --> 00:00:44.447
written by someone who lived in Illinois.

00:00:44.447 --> 00:00:46.596
You have to assume that the
person who wrote the diary

00:00:46.596 --> 00:00:48.615
probably, when they wrote it, had no idea

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.171
anyone would ever be reading it.

00:00:50.171 --> 00:00:52.023
I don't know what I'm gonna
find in these diaries.

00:00:52.023 --> 00:00:55.274
What if it's like "Dear
Diary, today I murdered."

00:00:55.274 --> 00:00:57.773
The starting price is $4.95, I'm gonna try

00:00:57.773 --> 00:01:00.695
bidding $6 and see what happens.

00:01:00.695 --> 00:01:02.677
Somebody else wants this diary.

00:01:02.677 --> 00:01:04.978
So I've been outbid and I'm in a bid war.

00:01:04.978 --> 00:01:09.407
I'm gonna increase my
maximum bid from $6 to $60.

00:01:09.407 --> 00:01:11.757
Hopefully it doesn't go up more from that.

00:01:11.757 --> 00:01:15.527
Two more people are trying
to bid on this diary.

00:01:15.527 --> 00:01:16.837
Things are getting intense.

00:01:16.837 --> 00:01:19.754
I bid $100 and somebody still beat me.

00:01:19.754 --> 00:01:24.375
I'm gonna have to play
hardball and I'm gonna bid $200

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:27.852
for this early 2000s diary from Illinois.

00:01:27.852 --> 00:01:30.648
Let's see how much it's
really worth to these people.

00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:33.065
I won, but I had to pay $160.

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:37.828
So, I drove up the price quite a bit.

00:01:37.828 --> 00:01:39.736
Let's hope there's some
murder in these diaries

00:01:39.736 --> 00:01:43.190
and not just like "Today I
ate another bowl of oatmeal."

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:45.462
These are the diaries of a stranger.

00:01:45.462 --> 00:01:46.420
Dream!

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.118
Whoa, this is very jam-packed
with a lot of handwriting.

00:01:50.118 --> 00:01:52.630
A lot of very small handwriting.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.492
We have no idea who wrote these,

00:01:54.492 --> 00:01:57.751
how old they were, what their gender was,

00:01:57.751 --> 00:01:59.433
we don't know if they're still alive.

00:01:59.433 --> 00:02:00.952
I'm gonna take a look inside

00:02:00.952 --> 00:02:04.073
and give 'em a read, and
I'll get back to you.

00:02:04.073 --> 00:02:06.622
This diary still has a pen attached,

00:02:06.622 --> 00:02:08.251
so this was probably the pen

00:02:08.251 --> 00:02:11.119
that this person used to write this.

00:02:11.119 --> 00:02:13.330
So, I emailed the eBay
seller to try to get

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.182
some more information on these diaries,

00:02:15.182 --> 00:02:17.961
and the person who sold them
definitely didn't write them.

00:02:17.961 --> 00:02:20.208
He said he bought them
from an estate sale.

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:24.257
That means that the person who
wrote them has possibly died.

00:02:24.257 --> 00:02:27.478
This might be a dead person's pen.

00:02:27.478 --> 00:02:29.969
This handwriting is
incredibly hard to read,

00:02:29.969 --> 00:02:31.969
so this is a challenge.

00:02:31.969 --> 00:02:34.559
"Thursday, January 4th, 2001.

00:02:34.559 --> 00:02:35.974
"Didn't sleep well last night.

00:02:35.974 --> 00:02:38.279
"Watched some TV then went to post office

00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:39.780
"and after that to Walmart.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.242
"Bought three plastic bins and SlimFast.

00:02:42.242 --> 00:02:43.391
"Home at one PM."

00:02:43.391 --> 00:02:46.220
I'm definitely getting the
impression that this is a woman.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.490
Even just reading the mundane
details of somebody's life,

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.602
it still feels very
personal to be reading it.

00:02:51.602 --> 00:02:54.710
So, this woman keeps writing
about someone named Micki,

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.189
and I really thought Micki was a baby,

00:02:57.189 --> 00:02:58.583
and I was like, why does this lady have

00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:01.522
a random baby in her house named Micki?

00:03:01.522 --> 00:03:04.282
And then I realized, Micki's a dog.

00:03:04.282 --> 00:03:05.942
Micki is a dog.
(bark)

00:03:05.942 --> 00:03:08.234
"Wednesday, February 7th, 2001.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:10.815
"Up at 8:30, Micki very
restless all night long."

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:13.204
The woman who wrote this
diary has had to endure

00:03:13.204 --> 00:03:16.184
some rude comments from
someone named Lydia,

00:03:16.184 --> 00:03:19.466
and I think Lydia is either
her stepmom or her sister,

00:03:19.466 --> 00:03:24.154
and basically Lydia said "You
don't wear clothes well."

00:03:24.154 --> 00:03:25.263
That's mean.

00:03:25.263 --> 00:03:27.522
And then she says "Your
stomach sticks out.

00:03:27.522 --> 00:03:28.922
"Your pants are too small."

00:03:28.922 --> 00:03:31.100
"Tuesday, January 9th, 2001.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.218
"Watched Oprah.

00:03:32.218 --> 00:03:34.410
"Friday, February 9th, 2001.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:36.810
"Slept well last night,
but had a lousy day.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.804
"All I wanted to do was sleep and eat."

00:03:38.804 --> 00:03:41.367
I've been reading the diary for days now

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.622
and, so far, no murders.

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.954
I'm starting to get the sense that

00:03:45.954 --> 00:03:48.774
there will be no murders in this diary.

00:03:48.774 --> 00:03:50.786
It's a lot of drinking SlimFast,

00:03:50.786 --> 00:03:52.594
a lot of going to Walmart,

00:03:52.594 --> 00:03:54.674
a lot of watching The Price is Right,

00:03:54.674 --> 00:03:56.383
but, hey, that's better than murdering,

00:03:56.383 --> 00:03:58.760
let's be honest, from a moral standpoint.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.729
Well, the handwriting is hard to read,

00:04:00.729 --> 00:04:04.079
but the more I read it, the
more I start to understand it.

00:04:04.079 --> 00:04:07.639
It's like my brain has
finally figured out the code.

00:04:07.639 --> 00:04:09.959
I'm in her head, she's in my head.

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:12.556
"Saturday, January 6th, 2001.

00:04:12.556 --> 00:04:14.537
"Up at 10:00, didn't sleep well.

00:04:14.537 --> 00:04:16.698
"Thursday, February 8th, 2001.

00:04:16.698 --> 00:04:18.026
"Didn't sleep again last night."

00:04:18.026 --> 00:04:20.255
She writes down what time she wakes up.

00:04:20.255 --> 00:04:22.586
She writes down whether
or not she slept well.

00:04:22.586 --> 00:04:24.346
Oftentimes, she doesn't sleep well.

00:04:24.346 --> 00:04:26.433
It's hard when you wake up in the morning

00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:29.232
and you feel like crap, and it sounds like

00:04:29.232 --> 00:04:30.794
that's happening a lot for her.

00:04:30.794 --> 00:04:32.531
Every single night she doesn't sleep well,

00:04:32.531 --> 00:04:36.132
it's just "Didn't sleep very
well," "Didn't sleep again,"

00:04:36.132 --> 00:04:38.594
"Didn't sleep well again,"
"Didn't sleep again."

00:04:38.594 --> 00:04:40.964
Every time she says "I finally
had a good night's sleep,"

00:04:40.964 --> 00:04:43.684
I'm like, good, good, finally!

00:04:43.684 --> 00:04:46.063
I feel deeply connected, and I want

00:04:46.063 --> 00:04:48.322
everything to be okay for this woman.

00:04:48.322 --> 00:04:52.183
She keeps talking about
someone named J.J. calling,

00:04:52.183 --> 00:04:56.100
and I think that J.J. could
be a son or a daughter.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.282
"Wednesday, January 10th, 2001.

00:04:58.282 --> 00:05:00.572
"J.J. didn't call today, I
should call him tomorrow."

00:05:00.572 --> 00:05:02.500
J.J., get it together!

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.588
Call your mom!

00:05:03.588 --> 00:05:07.188
I've just come across one
of the more exciting things

00:05:07.188 --> 00:05:11.308
that I have encountered in this
diary, and that's diarrhea.

00:05:11.308 --> 00:05:13.088
"October 10th, 2002.

00:05:13.088 --> 00:05:16.159
"I got up at 8:30, have diarrhea again."

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:20.537
I'm inspired by this because
I've written in a diary before

00:05:20.537 --> 00:05:22.820
and I don't think I would ever mention

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.755
that I have diarrhea, and
to be this comfortable

00:05:24.755 --> 00:05:28.484
with yourself, to say I
have diarrhea in your diary,

00:05:28.484 --> 00:05:31.342
I think we should all strive
to be that comfortable

00:05:31.342 --> 00:05:32.652
talking about diarrhea.

00:05:32.652 --> 00:05:35.643
Almost every day, she
writes "Woke up with Micki."

00:05:35.643 --> 00:05:37.893
Micki is mentioned almost every day.

00:05:37.893 --> 00:05:40.223
So, Micki seems like a good dog.

00:05:40.223 --> 00:05:42.973
She's running errands,
she stops at McDonald's,

00:05:42.973 --> 00:05:46.157
she gets two Happy Meals, one for herself

00:05:46.157 --> 00:05:49.225
and one for Micki, the dog.
(bark)

00:05:49.225 --> 00:05:52.077
I think she has an older father

00:05:52.077 --> 00:05:54.208
that she has to care for sometimes.

00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:56.542
"Tuesday, January 9th, 2001.

00:05:56.542 --> 00:05:58.782
"Dad went downstairs, so I tidied his room

00:05:58.782 --> 00:06:00.017
"and aired out his bed.

00:06:00.017 --> 00:06:01.730
"Read paper after Dad was finished.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.858
"Had juice and Dad and
I watched Price is Right

00:06:03.858 --> 00:06:05.209
"and then he ate his breakfast.

00:06:05.209 --> 00:06:06.829
"Lydia got up and I had SlimFast

00:06:06.829 --> 00:06:08.091
"while she had some oatmeal."

00:06:08.091 --> 00:06:10.929
I feel like what I'm learning
from reading these diaries,

00:06:10.929 --> 00:06:13.950
it's gonna sound cheesy, but I feel like

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:16.850
you can learn something from every person.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.222
There's not a bunch of exciting
stuff happening in here,

00:06:19.222 --> 00:06:20.811
there's nothing crazy, and yet,

00:06:20.811 --> 00:06:23.601
I still feel inspired by this woman.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.382
You know, she's writing down
all her personal thoughts

00:06:25.382 --> 00:06:27.123
and she never once says a negative thing

00:06:27.123 --> 00:06:31.290
about another person, and
she makes her bed every day,

00:06:32.848 --> 00:06:36.051
and I just feel like, I did not realize

00:06:36.051 --> 00:06:38.670
this was going to be such
an emotional roller coaster.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.529
I honestly did not.

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:43.238
And I would be so cranky if I
couldn't sleep all the time,

00:06:43.238 --> 00:06:46.870
and maybe she was, I haven't
found anything mean or cranky

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.931
written in five years' worth of diaries.

00:06:49.931 --> 00:06:51.913
I'm on the very last journal.

00:06:51.913 --> 00:06:55.982
In case you were wondering,
Micki is still alive and well

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:56.815
at the end.
(bark)

00:06:56.815 --> 00:07:01.331
The very last entry,
December 2nd, 2006, says

00:07:01.331 --> 00:07:05.870
"Slept pretty good, on the
couch by the fireplace."

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:10.037
I'm not gonna cry again,
I am not gonna cry again.

00:07:10.883 --> 00:07:13.550
(upbeat music)

